---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import PhoneCTA from '../../components/PhoneCTA.astro';
import SchemaMarkup from '../../components/SchemaMarkup.astro';
import { config } from '../../config';

const title = 'Medical & Lab Courier | Healthcare Specimen Transport Nanaimo';
const description = 'Specialized medical courier for lab specimens, pharmacy delivery, temperature-controlled transport. Chain-of-custody available. HIPAA-conscious service.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <SchemaMarkup type="Service" data={{ serviceName: 'Medical & Lab Courier', description }} />

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-navy to-brand-blue text-white py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="section-container">
      <h1 class="text-white mb-4">Medical & Lab Courier Service</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl opacity-95 mb-8 max-w-2xl">
        Specialized transport for lab specimens, pathology samples, pharmacy delivery. Temperature control, chain-of-custody, and healthcare-trained drivers.
      </p>
      <PhoneCTA text="Get Instant Quote" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Medical & Lab Courier Services</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="text-brand-blue mb-3">Specimen Transport</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Lab samples, blood draws, pathology specimens. Temperature-controlled insulated containers. Same-day delivery across Nanaimo and Vancouver Island.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="text-brand-blue mb-3">Pharmacy Delivery</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Prescription transfers, medication delivery to clinics and pharmacies. Confidential handling, signature required, proof of delivery.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="text-brand-blue mb-3">Chain-of-Custody</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Legal specimens, forensic samples, regulated transport. Full documentation, sealed containers, driver certification available.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="text-brand-blue mb-3">Medical Records</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Patient files, diagnostic reports, imaging records. Confidential delivery, secure containers, HIPAA-conscious protocols.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Temperature Control & Handling</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
      Not all medical cargo is the same. We provide appropriate transport based on specimen type:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Room Temperature (15–25°C)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Standard insulated container. Most routine labs, pharmacy picks, medical records.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Refrigerated (2–8°C)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Ice packs or gel packs. Blood cultures, some bacterial samples, vaccine transport.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Frozen (–20°C or lower)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Dry ice or ultra-cold containers. Plasma, tissue samples, specialized research specimens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Who We Serve</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Diagnostic Labs</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          Specimen pickup from clinics. Same-day turnaround. Nanaimo Island Health and private labs rely on us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Pharmacies</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          Prescription delivery, medication transfer, emergency stock runs across Vancouver Island.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Medical Clinics</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          Patient sample transport, urgent results delivery, inter-clinic transfers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Veterinary Clinics</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          Animal specimen transport to centralized labs. Temperature control, rapid turnaround.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Medical Courier Pricing</h2>

    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Medical transport starts at our standard rates, with surcharges for specialized handling:
      </p>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border border-gray-300 mb-6 space-y-3">
        <div class="pb-3 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Base Rate + Delivery</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Standard $18 base + $1.50/km (same as regular courier)</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-3 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Temperature Control</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">+$5–$15 depending on cooling method (ice packs to dry ice)</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-3 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Chain-of-Custody</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">+$20 for full documentation and certified handling</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Multiple Pickups</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">+$5 per additional clinic/location (volume discounts available)</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        Medical practices with regular volume? Ask about our monthly account rates and dedicated pickup schedules.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteForm />

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Medical Courier Workflow: Step-by-Step</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
      Here's exactly how we handle medical specimen delivery from your clinic to the lab:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Step 1: Specimen Preparation (Your Clinic)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Your clinic prepares specimen according to lab requirements: blood draws labeled with patient ID, urine samples in sterile containers, tissue samples in formalin, etc. You place in our provided sealed container with temperature-appropriate packing (ice packs for refrigerated, room temp for standard).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Step 2: We Pickup On Schedule</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Our driver arrives at your clinic at the agreed time (typically 3 PM daily, or custom timing). Driver scans container, photographs label, logs pickup time, and records chain-of-custody. You sign manifest; we email you a PDF receipt immediately.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Step 3: Temperature-Controlled Transit</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Specimen is placed in insulated vehicle with maintained temperature (ice packs refresh if long route). Driver tracks temperature with digital log (optional high-security biohazard runs include thermometer records). For Nanaimo local: 15–30 min transit. Victoria route: 3.5 hours (ferry-maintained).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Step 4: Lab Delivery & Chain-of-Custody Handoff</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Driver delivers to lab receiving desk, obtains signature + timestamp from lab technician, and photographs proof of delivery (container in lab's possession). Chain-of-custody form is completed with lab receipt time, condition notes ("Specimen arrived intact, temperature maintained"), and responsible person's name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Step 5: Confirmation & Documentation</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Within 30 minutes of delivery, you receive email with: proof-of-delivery photo, chain-of-custody summary, delivery timestamp, lab receipt confirmation. Your clinic records are complete for regulatory/audit purposes. Lab begins processing immediately.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Specimen Types We Handle Regularly</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Routine Labs</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Blood draws, urine samples, culture swabs. Room temperature (15–25°C). Most common; 30-min Nanaimo delivery.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Refrigerated Specimens</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Blood cultures, specific bacterial tests. Must stay 2–8°C. Ice packs + insulation. +$10 surcharge.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Pathology Slides</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Tissue biopsies, histology slides in formalin. Room temp, sealed containers. Fragile; careful handling required.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Frozen/Dry Ice Specimens</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Research samples, special stains, genetic testing. Must stay –20°C or colder. Dry ice containers. +$15 surcharge.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Pharmacy Delivery</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Prescription transfers, controlled substances (with appropriate documentation). Secure, signature-required delivery.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Medical Records & Imaging</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Patient files, X-rays, diagnostic imaging. Confidential, sealed envelopes. PIPEDA compliant.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Medical Courier FAQ</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Are your drivers trained in medical handling?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Our team is trained in specimen handling, chain-of-custody protocols, and confidentiality. We understand healthcare operations and regulatory requirements (PIPEDA, biohazard containment).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Can you do routine daily pickups?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Absolutely. Many clinics use us for daily 3 PM specimen runs. Standing orders, flat monthly rates ($80–$120/run), and volume discounts available. Fixed pickup time, no surprises.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">What's your turnaround for specimen delivery?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Local Nanaimo: 30 min–1 hour. Parksville/Comox: 2 hours. Victoria: 3.5–4 hours (ferry). Same-day guarantee on all routes if ordered by cutoff time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Do you handle hazardous/biohazard specimens?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes, with proper containment and training. We follow all Transport Canada and BC health regulations for biohazard transport. Specialized leak-proof containers included.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Is delivery confidential?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. All medical cargo is treated as confidential. No peeking, sealed containers, and driver discretion guaranteed. Your patient data stays secure with us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">What if a specimen arrives damaged?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Our chain-of-custody documentation captures condition at handoff. If damage occurs in transit, we photograph and notify you immediately. Temperature logs prove we maintained proper conditions. Work with your lab and clinic on next steps.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
